  "solution": "Given equation: 551 ÷ 19 − 16 × 12 + 121 = 100 \n\nExplanation:\n\nBODMAS rule\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f22f57d0cf5c493280a0ab6b7dbaea9e3fc5b035c6d410d59c2f476043bd03a8.png] \n\nInterchanging the signs and using BODMAS rule:\n\n1. − and ×\n\n**551 ÷ 19** × 16 − 12 + 121 = 100 \n\n**29 × 16** − 12 + 121 = 100\n\n**464** − 12 = 100\n\n**585 - 12** = 100\n\n573 ≠ 100\n\n2. + and ×\n\n**551 ÷ 19 **− 16 +12 × 121 = 100\n\n29 − 16 +**12 ×**** 121** = 100\n\n**29** − 16 **+1452 **= 100\n\n**1481 - 16 **= 100\n\n1465 ≠ 100\n\n3. ÷ and ×\n\n551 × 19 − **16 ÷ 12** + 121 = 100 \n\n**551 × 19** − 1.33 + 121 = 100\n\n**10469 − ****1.33 + 121 **= 100\n\n10588.67 ≠ 100\n\n**4. + and − **\n\n**551 ÷ 19** + 16 × 12 − 121 = 100 \n\n29 +**16 × 12** − 121 = 100 \n\n**29 + 192** - 121 = 100\n\n**221 - 121** = 100\n\n100 = 100\n\nHence,** \"Option 4\"** is the correct answer.",
